**How to implement.** The tests' fixture gains the store doubles that this section's re-point steps swap in, one for one, for the self-seeding stores S1.7 deletes (001 §B 'tests load the same files', 'the in-memory implementation stays as the test double'; .spec-md §3.3, §3.5). `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests) gains, each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S1.7: (1) `materialStore (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list) (versionsInUse : VersionsInUse) : MaterialProxy`, an empty `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty samplesReferencing versionsInUse` (`MaterialStore.fs`) holding every `materials ()` entry; (2) `sampleStore (versionsInUse : VersionsInUse) : SampleProxy`, an empty `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty versionsInUse` (`SampleStore.fs`) holding every `samples ()` sample; (3) `categoryStore (materialsReferencingCategory : CategoryId -> MaterialEntry list) : CategoryProxy`, an empty `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty materialsReferencingCategory` (`MaterialLibrary.fs`) holding every `categories ()` category; (4) `library () : LibraryProxy`, the `proxy` of an empty `Library.createInMemoryEmpty ()` store (`ElementId.fs:createInMemoryEmpty`) holding every sample as a `SampleItem` and then every `presets ()` entry, which is what the self-seeding `Library.createInMemory` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemory`, over `seedEntries`) serves today; (5) `sources () : SourcePreset list`, the `SourceItem` presets of `presets ()` in row order, and `source (id : ElementValueId) : SourcePreset`, which fails with the id when no source has it. Each store is filled through its own write verb (`saveMaterial`, `saveSample`, `addCategory`, `addEntry`) in the fixture's row order, and a refusal fails the calling fact with the refused entry and the error, as `freshStores` (step 41) does. Every call builds new stores, so no two facts share state. No cache beyond the one catalogue load, no seed value and no product change is added. (6) `BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests` gains `the fixture's store doubles hold the Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`: `materialStore (fun _ -> []) VersionsInUse.empty` lists exactly the ids of `materials ()` (`IncludeInactive`), `sampleStore VersionsInUse.empty` those of `samples ()` and `categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` those of `categories ()`; `library ()` resolves every sample's `entryId` and every preset to itself through `tryGetEntry`; `sources ()` holds exactly the `SourceItem` presets of `presets ()`, and `source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator` has tunable limits (`tunableLimitsOpt` matches `Some _`); and removing `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id` from one `sampleStore` leaves a second one holding it.

**Acceptance.** After the doubles land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture's store doubles hold the Built-in catalogue and are isolated per call`; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged, the linked fixture compiling in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
